{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB13036 - MONDO_6004",
  "verbalization": "Ramatroban is associated with Vasomotor Rhinitis through a series of indications that collectively suggest a potential mechanism of action. The evidence shows that Ramatroban is linked to Allergic Rhinitis, which in turn is indicated to treat Isoflupredone Acetate, Mebhydrolin, and Montelukast, all of which are known to be used for Vasomotor Rhinitis. This suggests that Ramatroban may share a common pathway in treating vasomotor rhinitis through the modulation of allergic responses. The presence of multiple overlapping indications points to a possible role in the pathophysiology of vasomotor rhinitis, possibly through anti-inflammatory or antihistaminic effects. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of considering the broader pharmacological context in evaluating Ramatroban's potential for repurposing in this condition.",
